# Walnut Linux Licensing

This repository contains components with different licenses:

## Kernel and kernel-related components

- **Kernel patches and configuration** (`packages/patched/kernel/linux/`):
  Distributed under the terms of the GNU General Public License version 2 only
  (GPL-2.0-only), matching the Linux kernel license.
- **RSX kernel driver** (`packages/walnut/drivers/ps3rsx/`):
  Kernel module code distributed under GPL-2.0-only.

## Our own code

Everything else written for this project (tools, the installer, packaging, system configuration
scripts, ps3-gpu-tools, the SPU code, benchmark and test harnesses) is distributed under the GNU
General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later version (GPL-2.0-or-later). The
full text of version 2 is at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.txt.

Third-party userland software packages and patches rebased on Debian source
packages retain their respective upstream licenses (e.g. Mesa, Plymouth,
games, and libraries).

## Artwork, logos, and media

- **Wallpapers** (`packages/walnut/system/ps3-desktop/files/backgrounds/`):
  - `walnut-sky.jpg` and `walnut-leaves.jpg`:
    Photographs of the walnut tree in the author's backyard.
    Copyright (c) 2026 Tiberiu Chibici.
    Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0
    International License (CC BY-NC 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/).
    See `packages/walnut/system/ps3-desktop/files/backgrounds/CREDITS` for details.
- **Logos and splash artwork** (`packages/walnut/system/ps3-splash/art/`):
  - Walnut Linux logo (`walnut-logo-light.svg`, `walnut-logo-dark.svg`, `walnut-mark.svg`):
    Procedural SVG design by the project authors / owner, generated by
    `packages/walnut/system/ps3-splash/art/make-logos.py`. License to be decided by the user with userland code.
  - Kernel boot logo (`packages/patched/kernel/linux/patches/local/0008`):
    Derived from the Walnut mark, distributed under GPL-2.0-only.
- **Other assets**:
  - Stand-in Plymouth progress glyphs (`eq.png`, `dot.png`, `nut.png`, `lbracket.png`, `rbracket.png`):
    Project procedural / stand-in artwork; license to be decided with userland code.
